3. Figure text-on-text overlap measurement (the check neither measure-figure-text nor
   check:figures performs; the cycle-1 accessibility pass was earned without it):
   logs-feat023-r2/figure-text-overlap.log + figure-text-overlap.json, instrument
   renders-feat023-r2/figure-text-overlap.mjs.
   Method: for each of the 16 EN variants the SERVED bytes were fetched and
   sha256-matched to the committed static/img bytes (servedMismatch=0), inlined into a
   blank page at natural viewBox size in headless Chromium; every <text> element's
   getBBox() was measured in SVG user units; pairwise bbox intersection was computed
   between all distinct text pairs (including the wordmark); every bbox-overlapping pair
   was then pixel-tested by rendering the SVG three times into canvases (element A alone,
   element B alone, all text hidden) and counting pixels inked in both A and B relative
   to the empty variant. The wordmark was additionally bbox-checked against every painted
   shape.
   RESULT: 14 of 16 variants have zero bbox-overlapping pairs and zero shared ink.
   fig-U2-3 (both variants) has two bbox-overlapping label pairs ("a verdict handed to
   a pupil" vs "the pupil, silently" 1.5x5; "travels and is never checked" vs "every
   later teacher" 13x4) that share ZERO ink pixels - box padding graze only, no visual
   superposition, not a defect.
